    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1123-a1">

                <pb facs="1022" n="708" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg708"/>


                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Colombian Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Suárez</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Chargé d’Affaires</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Bogotá</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 1, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Chargé d’Affaires</hi>: To-day’s papers publish
                    a telegram in which it is stated, with reference to officials of the Department
                    of State at Washington, that in the event of European nations sending
                    expeditions to South America to enforce strict neutrality on the part of those
                    countries, the Government of the United States would thereupon adopt a certain
                    line of conduct.</p>
                <p>In view of the source attributed to this news, I beg you kindly to inform me if
                    in your opinion it is worthy of credence.</p>
                <p>I renew [etc.]</p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marco Fidel Suárez</hi>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
